{
  "_about": "Stock loadouts for the 11 player aircraft, read off the original's Ammo Selection / configurator UI (user-supplied 2026-07-22). Hand-authored config describing the original game, NOT an extracted asset. Consumed by src/Flight/Weapons/Loadout.cs (M3 wave B, item B12).",
  "_references": "Mounts + binding rule: docs/formats/markers.md. Weapon ids + the caliber x ammo matrix: docs/formats/weapons.md. File format: docs/formats/loadouts.md.",
  "_ammo_types": {
    "slug": 0,
    "dumdum": 1,
    "ap": 2,
    "magnesium": 3
  },
  "_gun_resolves": "A gun's weapon id is caliber N + ammo index k -> wep_{N+k} (the wep_30..73 matrix, each caliber's four ammo types consecutive). Stock ammo 'slug' (k=0) gives wep_N: wep_30/40/50/60/70.",
  "_binding_rule": "gun slot n -> firepoint(9-2n),(10-2n); W1->fp7,8 W2->fp5,6 W3->fp3,4 W4->fp1,2. The 'markers' arrays below are the explicit result, checked into the file (not computed at runtime) so a wrong one is a visible fix. Strongly supported by geometry, pending in-engine confirmation (A10).",
  "_turrets": "Slots whose mount is a Turret carry \"turret\": true. Turrets are AI gunners (decision 10), deferred to M4: the loader parses them but constructs them inert. Filled on the 5 turret airframes; the Balmoral is the only two-turret airframe (Nose + Rear).",
  "_selectable": "The Ammo Selection screen's two dropdowns, in the original's own order, read off OriginalScreenshots/'Ammo Selection Gun DropDown.png' and 'Ammo Selection Hardpoint DropDown.png'. NOT derivable from the weapon tiers: the incendiary wep_04 is a named weapon the screen does not offer, and the rocket order is not id order. There is no per-airframe, per-hardpoint or budget restriction on what may be fitted (user, holding the original). Labels are the dropdown's own words, which is why magnesium reads 'Explosive'.",
  "selectable": {
    "gun_ammo": [
      { "id": "slug", "label": "Slug" },
